        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/n/4/glastonbury-abbey-wp/alleged-burial-site-of-king-ar.jpg",
          "filename": "Alleged Burial Site of King Arthur (6337078108).jpg",
          "caption": "After the crucifixion of Jesus lore has it that Joseph of Arimathea (who according to the Bible donated his own tomb for Christ's interment after the Crucifixion) came to Britain, bearing the Holy Grail - the cup used by Christ at the Last Supper and later by Joseph to catch his blood at the crucifixion.\nWhen Joseph landed on the island of Avalon, he set foot on Wearyall Hill - just below the Tor. Exhausted, he thrust his staff into the ground, and rested. By morning, his staff had taken root - leaving a strange oriental thorn bush - the sacred Glastonbury Thorn.\n\nFor safe keeping, Joseph is said to have buried the Holy Grail just below the Tor at the entrance to the Underworld. Shortly after he had done this, a spring, now known as Chalice Well, flowed forth and the water that emerged brought eternal youth to whosoever would drink it.",
          "alt": "After the crucifixion of Jesus lore has it that Joseph of Arimathea (who according to the Bible donated his own tomb for Christ's interment after the Crucifixion) came to Britain, bearing the Holy Grail - the cup used by Christ at the Last Supper and later by Joseph to catch his blood at the crucifixion.\nWhen Joseph landed on the island of Avalon, he set foot on Wearyall Hill - just below the Tor. Exhausted, he thrust his staff into the ground, and rested. By morning, his staff had taken root - leaving a strange oriental thorn bush - the sacred Glastonbury Thorn.\n\nFor safe keeping, Joseph is said to have buried the Holy Grail just below the Tor at the entrance to the Underworld. Shortly after he had done this, a spring, now known as Chalice Well, flowed forth and the water that emerged brought eternal youth to whosoever would drink it.",
          "width": 990,
          "height": 655,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Lies Thru a Lens ",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alleged_Burial_Site_of_King_Arthur_(6337078108).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
